# Published archive keeps only lib/, example/, doc/, skills/, README.md,
# CHANGELOG.md, LICENSE, and pubspec.yaml. Everything below is dev/CI/test
# tooling that must not ship to pub.dev.
#
# ANCHORING IS LOAD-BEARING. .pubignore uses gitignore semantics, so a BARE
# `config/` matches a directory named `config` at ANY DEPTH — including
# `lib/src/config/`. That is exactly how diene_auth_engine 1.0.0 and 1.0.1
# shipped WITHOUT `lib/src/config/auth_engine_config.dart` while
# `lib/diene_auth_engine.dart` line 22 still exports it: both archives are
# structurally unusable, every consumer fails to compile with
# "Type 'AuthEngineConfig' not found", and publication is irreversible.
# The same hazard applies to every root-only directory below. Anchoring makes
# each exclusion mean exactly the repository layer it names.
/.claude/
/.dart_tool/
/.direnv/
/.github/
/.kagent/
/.kloop/
/config/
/coverage/
/docs/
/nix/
/scripts/
/tasks/
/test/
/tool/
.coderabbit.yaml
.envrc
.markdownlint-cli2.jsonc
.prettierrc.yaml
codecov.yml
dlint.yaml
flake.lock
flake.nix
release.yaml
Taskfile.yaml
CLAUDE.md
VERSION
